{%- comment -%}
  vf-design-credit — mandated per Leora License Schedule A, bound
  via §7.2 of the master agreement (legal/leora-license/agreement.pdf).

  Renders the exact contract-mandated string "Design by Leora" on any
  PDP where product.metafields.vox.design_origin.value | downcase
  equals the literal 'leora'. Anywhere else, renders nothing.

  Contract rules — do NOT alter without legal review:

    - EXACT STRING hardcoded: "Design by Leora". Never derived from
      the metafield value. The metafield value is a lookup key
      (currently "leora"); the credit is the contract-mandated
      wording verbatim. No variants, no abbreviations, no
      stylisation, no translation, no case changes.

    - Value-gate, never presence-gate. A future third-party creator
      with their own metafield value (e.g. "studio-foo") MUST NOT
      inherit Leora's credit. The downcase compare against the
      literal 'leora' enforces this: any other value falls through.

    - §5.5 nominative use: plain text only. No Leora logo, no Brand
      Elements, no framing as collaboration, partnership, or
      endorsement. Just the credit line.

    - Never nested inside a collapsible_tab or any interaction-gated
      container. Schedule A requires "reasonably visible font size"
      without burial. This snippet is rendered from sections/main-
      product.liquid's {%- when 'description' -%} case handler, which
      sits in the block loop above every collapsible_tab in the
      current block_order — visible without interaction.

    - Atelier exclusion (contract §5.5, endorsement misrepresentation
      risk): Atelier products are original Voxel Forge work and MUST
      NOT carry the Leora credit. The value-gate handles this — no
      Atelier product carries vox.design_origin = 'leora' in admin.
      Do not introduce a presence-based fallback.

  Placement: rendered from sections/main-product.liquid inside the
  existing {%- when 'description' -%} case handler, immediately after
  the description <div> closes. The render deliberately does NOT live
  in a custom_liquid block in templates/product.json — the Shopify
  Theme Editor autonomously rewrites .json template files on Customizer
  edits (demonstrated live by auto-commit c484bf93 on 2026-07-12,
  which rewrote templates/index.json between two of our deploys).
  A dropped block would re-enter Schedule A breach with §12.1
  termination exposure invisibly, so the render was moved into Dawn-
  native Liquid source (which the Theme Editor does not rewrite) by
  commit aacaf381 on 2026-07-14. See CLAUDE.md §9 "Dawn-native section
  modification: sanctioned exceptions" for the §2-exception ledger.

  CSS: assets/vf-tokens.css §27.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign _origin = product.metafields.vox.design_origin.value | downcase -%}
{%- if _origin == 'leora' -%}
  <p class="vf-design-credit">Design by Leora</p>
{%- endif -%}
